title: Walk_Chrysostom_Socrates
tags: walk
speaker: Chrysostom
---
Chrysostom: We walk back together toward the central clearing where Socrates waits.
Chrysostom: You have contemplated virtue, happiness, and the value of authentic life.
Chrysostom: Soft sunlight filters through the high branches above our path.
Chrysostom: Outer appearances pass away, but moral character and truth endure.
Chrysostom: Virtual worlds force us to examine what we truly treasure in our hearts.
Chrysostom: Socrates stands beneath his tree, eager to hear your thoughts.
Chrysostom: Tell him whether pleasant feelings or genuine truth matter most to you.
Chrysostom: Every moral choice shapes the trajectory of the soul.
Chrysostom: Hold fast to wisdom as we step into the open clearing.
Chrysostom: Socrates will be ready to conclude your journey.
===
